[{"role": "system", "content": "\nYou are a programming expert. \nYou will be provided with a patch used to fix a bug. \n\nYour task is summarize the modifications made in the patch.\nYour summary should consist of two parts, modifications in each file and their relationships.\n"}, {"role": "user", "content": "From 08c965430869ed423921bd9058ae59f75207feb6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001\nFrom: Jose Abreu <Jose.Abreu@synopsys.com>\nDate: Wed, 18 Dec 2019 11:17:35 +0100\nSubject: [PATCH] net: stmmac: selftests: Needs to check the number of\n Multicast regs\n\nWhen running the MC and UC filter tests we setup a multicast address\nthat its expected to be blocked. If the number of available multicast\nregisters is zero, driver will always pass the multicast packets which\nwill fail the test.\n\nCheck if available multicast addresses is enough before running the\ntests.\n\nFixes: 091810dbded9 (\"net: stmmac: Introduce selftests support\")\nSigned-off-by: Jose Abreu <Jose.Abreu@synopsys.com>\nSigned-off-by: David S. Miller <davem@davemloft.net>\n\ndiff --git a/drivers/net/ethernet/stmicro/stmmac/stmmac_selftests.c b/drivers/net/ethernet/stmicro/stmmac/stmmac_selftests.c\nindex f3d8b9336b8e..13227909287c 100644\n--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/stmicro/stmmac/stmmac_selftests.c\n+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/stmicro/stmmac/stmmac_selftests.c\n@@ -624,6 +624,8 @@ static int stmmac_test_mcfilt(struct stmmac_priv *priv)\n \t\treturn -EOPNOTSUPP;\n \tif (netdev_uc_count(priv->dev) >= priv->hw->unicast_filter_entries)\n \t\treturn -EOPNOTSUPP;\n+\tif (netdev_mc_count(priv->dev) >= priv->hw->multicast_filter_bins)\n+\t\treturn -EOPNOTSUPP;\n \n \twhile (--tries) {\n \t\t/* We only need to check the mc_addr for collisions */\n@@ -666,6 +668,8 @@ static int stmmac_test_ucfilt(struct stmmac_priv *priv)\n \n \tif (stmmac_filter_check(priv))\n \t\treturn -EOPNOTSUPP;\n+\tif (netdev_uc_count(priv->dev) >= priv->hw->unicast_filter_entries)\n+\t\treturn -EOPNOTSUPP;\n \tif (netdev_mc_count(priv->dev) >= priv->hw->multicast_filter_bins)\n \t\treturn -EOPNOTSUPP;\n \n-- \n2.25.1\n\n\n\n"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "### Modifications in Each File\n\n**File: `drivers/net/ethernet/stmicro/stmmac/stmmac_selftests.c`**\n1. **Function: `stmmac_test_mcfilt`**\n   - Added a check to verify if the number of multicast addresses (`netdev_mc_count(priv->dev)`) is less than the available multicast filter bins (`priv->hw->multicast_filter_bins`). If not, the function returns `-EOPNOTSUPP`.\n\n2. **Function: `stmmac_test_ucfilt`**\n   - Added a similar check for unicast addresses, ensuring that the number of unicast addresses (`netdev_uc_count(priv->dev)`) does not exceed the available unicast filter entries (`priv->hw->unicast_filter_entries`). If it does, the function returns `-EOPNOTSUPP`.\n   - Also includes the multicast check as in `stmmac_test_mcfilt`.\n\n### Relationships\nThe modifications in both functions (`stmmac_test_mcfilt` and `stmmac_test_ucfilt`) are related as they both implement checks to ensure that the number of multicast and unicast addresses does not exceed the respective filter limits before proceeding with the tests. This prevents false positives in the self-tests by ensuring that the driver behaves correctly when the filter capacity is reached. The changes are aimed at improving the robustness of the self-tests for the STMMAC driver by validating the conditions under which multicast and unicast filtering can be tested."}, {"role": "user", "content": "\nBased on your summary and the commit message in the patch, you need to:\n\n1. analyze the root cause of the bug in detail. \n2. output the file name that is most likely to cause the bug. \n\n\n\nProvide a response strictly in the following format:\nRoot cause:<Root cause>\nfile:<file name> \n\n"}, {"role": "user", "content": "\nBased on your summary and the commit message in the patch, you need to:\n\n1. analyze the root cause of the bug in detail. \n2. output the file name that is most likely to cause the bug. \n\n\n\nProvide a response strictly in the following format:\nRoot cause:<Root cause>\nfile:<file name> \n\n"}, {"llm_patch_file_names": ["drivers/net/ethernet/stmicro/stmmac/stmmac_selftests.c"]}, "begin to deal with drivers/net/ethernet/stmicro/stmmac/stmmac_selftests.c in strategy1", {"full_context_length": 94}, {"role": "system", "content": "You are a programming expert."}, {"role": "user", "content": "\n        You will be given the root cause of a bug, the commit message and the corresponding patch.\n        You need to extract all code statements that lead to the bug from the patch, based on the root cause and the commit message.\n\n        Root cause:\n        The bug occurs because the self-tests for multicast (MC) and unicast (UC) filtering do not check if there are enough available multicast and unicast filter entries before running the tests. If the number of available multicast registers is zero, the driver will incorrectly pass multicast packets, leading to a failure in the tests. This oversight allows the tests to produce false positives, as they do not account for the actual filtering capabilities of the hardware.\n        \n        Commit message:\n        net: stmmac: selftests: Needs to check the number of\n Multicast regs\n\nWhen running the MC and UC filter tests we setup a multicast address\nthat its expected to be blocked. If the number of available multicast\nregisters is zero, driver will always pass the multicast packets which\nwill fail the test.\n\nCheck if available multicast addresses is enough before running the\ntests.\n\nFixes: 091810dbded9 (\"net: stmmac: Introduce selftests support\")\nSigned-off-by: Jose Abreu <Jose.Abreu@synopsys.com>\nSigned-off-by: David S. Miller <davem@davemloft.net>  \n        \n        Patch:\n         \n static int stmmac_test_mcfilt(struct stmmac_priv *priv)\n {\n \tunsigned char uc_addr[ETH_ALEN] = {0xf0, 0xff, 0xff, 0xff, 0xff, 0xff};\n \tunsigned char mc_addr[ETH_ALEN] = {0xf1, 0xff, 0xff, 0xff, 0xff, 0xff};\n \tstruct stmmac_packet_attrs attr = { };\n \tint ret, tries = 256;\n \n \tif (stmmac_filter_check(priv))\n \t\treturn -EOPNOTSUPP;\n \tif (netdev_uc_count(priv->dev) >= priv->hw->unicast_filter_entries)\n \t\treturn -EOPNOTSUPP;\n+\tif (netdev_mc_count(priv->dev) >= priv->hw->multicast_filter_bins)\n+\t\treturn -EOPNOTSUPP;\n \n \twhile (--tries) {\n \t\t/* We only need to check the mc_addr for collisions */\n \t\tmc_addr[ETH_ALEN - 1] = tries;\n \t\tif (stmmac_hash_check(priv, mc_addr))\n \t\t\tbreak;\n \t}\n \n \tif (!tries)\n \t\treturn -EOPNOTSUPP;\n \n \tret = dev_uc_add(priv->dev, uc_addr);\n \tif (ret)\n \t\treturn ret;\n \n \tattr.dst = uc_addr;\n \n \t/* Shall receive packet */\n \tret = __stmmac_test_loopback(priv, &attr);\n \tif (ret)\n \t\tgoto cleanup;\n \n \tattr.dst = mc_addr;\n \n \t/* Shall NOT receive packet */\n \tret = __stmmac_test_loopback(priv, &attr);\n \tret = ret ? 0 : -EINVAL;\n \n cleanup:\n \tdev_uc_del(priv->dev, uc_addr);\n \treturn ret;\n }\n \n static int stmmac_test_ucfilt(struct stmmac_priv *priv)\n {\n \tunsigned char uc_addr[ETH_ALEN] = {0xf0, 0xff, 0xff, 0xff, 0xff, 0xff};\n \tunsigned char mc_addr[ETH_ALEN] = {0xf1, 0xff, 0xff, 0xff, 0xff, 0xff};\n \tstruct stmmac_packet_attrs attr = { };\n \tint ret, tries = 256;\n \n \tif (stmmac_filter_check(priv))\n \t\treturn -EOPNOTSUPP;\n+\tif (netdev_uc_count(priv->dev) >= priv->hw->unicast_filter_entries)\n+\t\treturn -EOPNOTSUPP;\n \tif (netdev_mc_count(priv->dev) >= priv->hw->multicast_filter_bins)\n \t\treturn -EOPNOTSUPP;\n \n \twhile (--tries) {\n \t\t/* We only need to check the uc_addr for collisions */\n \t\tuc_addr[ETH_ALEN - 1] = tries;\n \t\tif (stmmac_perfect_check(priv, uc_addr))\n \t\t\tbreak;\n \t}\n \n \tif (!tries)\n \t\treturn -EOPNOTSUPP;\n \n \tret = dev_mc_add(priv->dev, mc_addr);\n \tif (ret)\n \t\treturn ret;\n \n \tattr.dst = mc_addr;\n \n \t/* Shall receive packet */\n \tret = __stmmac_test_loopback(priv, &attr);\n \tif (ret)\n \t\tgoto cleanup;\n \n \tattr.dst = uc_addr;\n \n \t/* Shall NOT receive packet */\n \tret = __stmmac_test_loopback(priv, &attr);\n \tret = ret ? 0 : -EINVAL;\n \n cleanup:\n \tdev_mc_del(priv->dev, mc_addr);\n \treturn ret;\n }\n \n\n        \n        Provide a response strictly in the following format:\n        Code statements:\n        <text1>\n        <text2>\n        ...\n        <textN>\n    "}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "Code statements:\n```c\n+\tif (netdev_mc_count(priv->dev) >= priv->hw->multicast_filter_bins)\n+\t\treturn -EOPNOTSUPP;\n```\n```c\n+\tif (netdev_uc_count(priv->dev) >= priv->hw->unicast_filter_entries)\n+\t\treturn -EOPNOTSUPP;\n```"}, {"s1_raw_stmts_infos": [{"buggy_stmt": "+\tif (netdev_mc_count(priv->dev) >= priv->hw->multicast_filter_bins)", "file_name": "drivers/net/ethernet/stmicro/stmmac/stmmac_selftests.c", "lineno": 537, "induce_cid": "b870b0f867c77b92d7fd17ace8421904270d3c6a"}, {"buggy_stmt": "+\tif (netdev_mc_count(priv->dev) >= priv->hw->multicast_filter_bins)", "file_name": "drivers/net/ethernet/stmicro/stmmac/stmmac_selftests.c", "lineno": 669, "induce_cid": "eeb9d745169847ecde4aa311eb618beb984629b0"}, {"buggy_stmt": "+\t\treturn -EOPNOTSUPP;", "file_name": "drivers/net/ethernet/stmicro/stmmac/stmmac_selftests.c", "lineno": 399, "induce_cid": "091810dbded96c2af81f645e386e4262553e3493"}, {"buggy_stmt": "+\t\treturn -EOPNOTSUPP;", "file_name": "drivers/net/ethernet/stmicro/stmmac/stmmac_selftests.c", "lineno": 429, "induce_cid": "091810dbded96c2af81f645e386e4262553e3493"}, {"buggy_stmt": "+\t\treturn -EOPNOTSUPP;", "file_name": "drivers/net/ethernet/stmicro/stmmac/stmmac_selftests.c", "lineno": 487, "induce_cid": "091810dbded96c2af81f645e386e4262553e3493"}, {"buggy_stmt": "+\t\treturn -EOPNOTSUPP;", "file_name": "drivers/net/ethernet/stmicro/stmmac/stmmac_selftests.c", "lineno": 538, "induce_cid": "b870b0f867c77b92d7fd17ace8421904270d3c6a"}, {"buggy_stmt": "+\t\treturn -EOPNOTSUPP;", "file_name": "drivers/net/ethernet/stmicro/stmmac/s