e4aa311eb618beb984629b0"]}, {"role": "system", "content": "You are a programming expert."}, {"role": "user", "content": "\n        You are a programming expert.\n        You will be given the root cause of a bug and some code statements that lead to the bug.\n        Rank these code statements based on their relevance to the root cause of the bug.\n        \n        Root cause:\n        The bug occurs because the self-tests for multicast (MC) and unicast (UC) filtering do not check if there are enough available multicast and unicast filter entries before running the tests. If the number of available multicast registers is zero, the driver will incorrectly pass multicast packets, leading to a failure in the tests. This oversight allows the tests to produce false positives, as they do not account for the actual filtering capabilities of the hardware.\n        \n        code statements:\n        +\tif (netdev_mc_count(priv->dev) >= priv->hw->multicast_filter_bins)\n+\t\treturn -EOPNOTSUPP;\n+\tif (netdev_uc_count(priv->dev) >= priv->hw->unicast_filter_entries)\n+\t\treturn -EOPNOTSUPP;\n  \n\n        Provide a response strictly in the following format:\n        Ranked Code statements:\n        <text1>\n        <text2>\n        ...\n        <textN>\n        ...\n    "}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "Code statements:\n```c\n+\tif (netdev_mc_count(priv->dev) >= priv->hw->multicast_filter_bins)\n+\t\treturn -EOPNOTSUPP;\n```\n```c\n+\tif (netdev_uc_count(priv->dev) >= priv->hw->unicast_filter_entries)\n+\t\treturn -EOPNOTSUPP;\n```"}, {"s1_ranked_stmts_infos": [{"buggy_stmt": "```", "file_name": "drivers/net/ethernet/stmicro/stmmac/stmmac_selftests.c", "lineno": 537, "induce_cid": "b870b0f867c77b92d7fd17ace8421904270d3c6a"}, {"buggy_stmt": "```", "file_name": "drivers/net/ethernet/stmicro/stmmac/stmmac_selftests.c", "lineno": 669, "induce_cid": "eeb9d745169847ecde4aa311eb618beb984629b0"}, {"buggy_stmt": "```", "file_name": "drivers/net/ethernet/stmicro/stmmac/stmmac_se